  "explain": {
   "text": "Fractions add only once they count the same piece.[^1] Half an hour plus three-quarters: 1/2 is 2/4, so 2/4 + 3/4 = 5/4, an hour and a quarter, 75 minutes. Add the tops and keep the bottom.[^2] Taking away works the same: 3/4 − 2/4 = 1/4, 15 minutes.[^3]\n\nThe trap is adding top and bottom: 1/2 + 3/4 = 4/6. That is 40 minutes, less than the 45 you started with.\n\n**Match the piece, then add the tops and keep the bottom: 1/2 + 3/4 = 5/4.**"
  },
  "analogy": {
   "text": "You never add 750 mm and 1.5 m as 751.5. Put both in millimetres: 750 + 1500 = 2250 mm.",
   "breaks": "A metre is always 1000 mm; with fractions you choose the piece and check it measures both."
  },
  "practice": {
   "text": "**Rule of thumb:** same piece first; then tops add and the bottom stays.\n\n**Worked example:** visits of 1 3/4 and 2 1/2 hours. 1 + 2 = 3, and 3/4 + 2/4 = 5/4 = 1 1/4. Total 4 1/4 hours.\n\n**Common mistakes**\n- Adding the bottoms: 1/2 + 3/4 as 4/6.\n- Adding the tops before matching the piece."
  },
